  "facts": [
    "Pulaski Bridge, a 1954 bascule drawbridge, spans Newtown Creek, LIRR tracks, and the Queens‑Midtown Tunnel entrance, carrying six traffic lanes and a pedestrian sidewalk that overlooks Manhattan’s skyline.",
    "Reconstructed from 1991 to 1994, the bridge now features a dedicated two‑way bike lane, opened April 2016 after overcoming challenges posed by its movable leaves and lightweight dividers.",
    "Named for Polish commander Casimir Pulaski, the bridge honors Greenpoint’s large Polish‑American community and once displayed John Fekner’s 1979–1990 mural, “Wheels Over Indian Trails.”"
  ],
